not `charge under s 420` with `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only` 's `made out`
`charge under s 420` with `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only` 's `text` is equal to 
`charge under s 420` with `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only` 's `refusal` is equal to A charge under section 420 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: dishonestly (section 420 requires dishonesty; fraud alone is section 417).
`charge under s 417` with `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only` 's `text` is equal to You, Christine Lewis, are charged that you, on or about the 24th day of April 2000, at about 8.10 pm, at the Seiyu Departmental Store at Parkway Parade Shopping Centre, Singapore, did cheat one Wong Fei Hsia, the cashier of Seiyu Departmental Store by deceiving her to believe that the price of a "Pochacco" pencil casing is worth $5.25, when in actual fact, you knew that the price of the said item is worth $16.95, and by such manner of deception, you fraudulently induced the said Wong Fei Hsia to deliver to you the said item for only $5.25 which she would not have done, had she not been so deceived, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 417 of the Penal Code 1871.
